# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""037.md batch Y: deepen vv 64, 120, 121, 171.

All four bodies were verified correct against their own verses before rewriting,
so this is depth work only. Each is written on a different portion of the shared
apparatus so it does not duplicate a neighbour:

  v64  takes the location and the two descriptions of the tree (roots from the
       bottom of Hell, nourished by fire, IK; roots at the depths with branches
       rising through the levels, Z). v63 covers the trial and v65 the spathes.
  v120 takes the pronouncement itself and the distinctive pairing of two
       prophets in a single salutation. v119 (batch U) already covers the
       blessing left upon a pair and the formula's occasions.
  v121 takes the refrain's fourth occurrence and what distinguishes it: it
       closes the one account that ends in a blessing rather than a trial.
       v80 (batch T) covers 29:69c and the reward-of-goodness principle, v110
       the parallel list, and v131 (batch W) the fifth occurrence, so none of
       that is repeated.
  v171 takes the phrase "has already gone forth" and the nature of the Word as
       already issued. v172 covers the helping and IK's ground at 40:51-52, and
       v173 the victory and the decree at 58:21, so neither is repeated.

Guards: no verbatim re-quote of the verse in the opening prose; no verbatim
repeat of blockquote wording in the prose above it; echo the verse's own
distinctive vocabulary; paragraphs distinct so duprate stays under 0.025.
"""

SURAH = "al-Ṣaffāt"
